1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,027
Part one is A2UI. Its key idea is that the layout and the data are sent separately, and components bind to data by path.

2
00:00:10,027 --> 00:00:21,128
The four envelope messages. A surface must exist first; updateComponents sends a flat list where components reference each other by id.

3
00:00:21,128 --> 00:00:34,166
The Surface keeps a component map and a data model. resolve() turns {path: ...} bindings into values, and tree() turns the flat map into the normalized tree. Ids that have not arrived yet render as placeholders.

4
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:45,202
STATIC mode: the templates are ours. The model only chooses 'sales_overview' and returns values; our code sends every component.

5
00:00:45,202 --> 00:00:57,227
DECLARATIVE, OPEN-ENDED and MIXED: the model writes A2UI JSONL. Each complete line is applied and checked before it is forwarded, so the page can render while the model is still writing.

6
00:00:57,227 --> 00:01:08,264
Here is what the model sends in declarative mode: components first, data afterwards. The title is a binding to /title, and it fills in when updateDataModel arrives.

7
00:01:08,264 --> 00:01:20,295
Actions: a click sends an A2UI action. The model designs the detail surface with bindings only, and then the app supplies the real numbers with updateDataModel.

8
00:01:20,295 --> 00:01:36,379
Running it in the terminal: each message, then the click, then the same tree drawn by a terminal renderer.

9
00:01:36,379 --> 00:01:47,562
Static: the model only chose the template. The wire log shows our fixed updateComponents followed by one updateDataModel.

10
00:01:47,562 --> 00:02:00,719
Declarative: watch the components stream in. Then I click 'West details', which creates a second surface designed by the model and filled with data by the app.

11
00:02:00,719 --> 00:02:12,889
Open-ended: a single HtmlView holds model-written HTML in a sandbox. Clicking a legend row sends an action out through postMessage.

12
00:02:12,889 --> 00:02:25,046
Mixed: catalog KPIs and chart, plus one sandboxed what-if slider, which is something the catalog cannot express.

13
00:02:25,046 --> 00:02:35,195
The A2UI tests cover bindings, rejected envelopes, the template ownership in static mode, and the action round trip.

